answer:
If I were to choose my own special dinner guests, I would pick:
1. Alexander the Great - the famous conqueror and king of Macedonia;
2. Emperor Wu of Han - the long-reigning Chinese emperor who established a powerful empire known as the "Prosperous Age of Emperor Wu";
3. Emperor Taizong of Tang - the second emperor of the Tang dynasty, known for his great governance and cultural prosperity;
4. Genghis Khan - the founder of the Mongol Empire and considered one of the most influential and successful military leaders in history;
5. Kublai Khan - the grandson of Genghis Khan and the founder of the Yuan Dynasty in China, which was at its height under his rule.

I chose these figures because they have all made significant contributions to their respective worlds and had a profound impact on world history. At this dinner party, we could discuss the reasons for their success and the challenges they faced.

Sure! I would pick:  
• Confucius — the philosopher himself, whose teachings are at the foundation of many aspects of Chinese culture and society;  
• Li Bai (Li Po in Wade-Giles) — the famous Tang dynasty poet who is considered a national treasure in China, alongside Du Fu he defines the classical canon of Chinese poetry;  
• Zhang Heng — the inventor of the first seismograph, as well as an accomplished poet and artist of his time;  
• Zu Chongzhi — the mathematician who calculated pi with great precision and also was involved in the fields of mechanical engineering, astronomy, and calendar systems in his lifetime;  
• Zu Geng — Zu Chongzhi's son who made contributions to mathematics and astronomy, including his father's work on Pi.
